FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: an-imperial-message.
OFF THE RECORD: Start a child case, publish a message to the gazette, then use
OFF THE RECORD: discovery to confirm that the child received it.

ARTICLE 1.
    COMMENCE PROCEEDINGS UPON "FORM K-1. IN THE MATTER OF: you-the-subject. ARTICLE 1. AWAIT THE GAZETTE, FILED UNDER message. LET IT BE RECORDED THAT received IS message. ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.", FILED UNDER subject.
    PUBLISH "a message from the emperor, whispered to the messenger, confirmed in your ear" IN THE GAZETTE.
    ADJOURN FOR 2 DAYS.

ARTICLE 2.
    PROCLAIM "the subject, per discovery, received: " PLUS THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE RECORD received IN THE MATTER OF subject.
    PROCLAIM "the message has arrived. This is not canon, but it is on the record.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
